/**
\page org_mitk_views_headmotioncorrectionview Head-Motion Correction

This view corrects head motion and eddy-current distortions in a diffusion-weighted image (DWI).
The reference is the first volume of the shell with the lowest b-value, usually a b0 volume. Every
other volume is registered to it with an affine transformation (MatchPoint's multi-modal affine
algorithm) and resampled with B-spline interpolation. The gradient direction of each volume is
rotated with the rotation part of its transformation. The corrected DWI keeps the volume order of
the input and appears below it, named "_Corrected".

The correction runs in the background, so MITK stays usable meanwhile; it takes about as many
registrations as the DWI has volumes. If it fails, a message shows the reason.
*/
